</p/><p><strong>Summary: </strong>
I&rsquo;m excited to be bringing #MythicBastionland to #UCon in Ypsilanti.
</p>
        <p>I’ve signed up to attend and facilitate games at <a href="https://www.ucon-gaming.org/">U-Con Gaming Convention – Nov
13-15, 2026</a> in Ypsilanti Michigan.</p>
<p>I’ve chosen to run three sessions of <cite><a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/514996/mythic-bastionland?affiliate_id=318171">Mythic Bastionland</a></cite> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Mythic Bastionland”" title="Other site-wide references of “Mythic Bastionland”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-MYTHIC-BASTIONLAND">&#128214;</a></small>
.  Which can be found on
the <a href="https://tabletop.events/conventions/u-con-2026/schedule#?query=Seek%20the%20Myths%20Honour&amp;filter_liked=0&amp;day_id=&amp;eventtype_id=&amp;startdaypart_id=">Schedule of Events</a>.  The description of the game, a poem as follows:</p>
<p class="verse">
Fresh oaths fall from green tongue<br />
Upon slumbering dream-weary realm<br />
“Awake!” bursts from most-foul seer lung<br />
The myths stir and march to overwhelm<br />
</p>
<p>I’m envisioning this as sessions that will build upon each other.  Players can
continue to play their knights from one session to another; while also allowing
for new players to join.</p>
<p>I opted for a 4 hour slot, as I wanted to ensure that if we’re all having a good
time we can keep on rocking it.  I also deliberately limited it to 4 players, as
larger tables just don’t do it for me.  And I set the floor at 1 player, because
frankly <cite>Mythic Bastionland</cite>
 works quite well with one player.</p>
<p>I haven’t run a convention game in a few years, and am looking forward to the
energy I find these games bringing.</p>

